.TH DOLPHIN-CLEAN-TITLE 1 "September 2026" "Dolphin Clean Title 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dolphin-clean-title \- remove the Dolphin suffix from X11 window titles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dolphin-clean-title
.RB [ \-\-background | \-\-foreground | \-\-stop | \-\-status | \-\-diagnose | ui ]
.br
.B dolphin-clean-title
.RB { enable | disable | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dolphin-clean-title
rewrites a matching trailing \(em Dolphin or - Dolphin suffix from Dolphin
window titles before X11 window lists and taskbars display them.
.PP
The feature uses a user-local Dolphin launcher and an X11/XWayland title
cleaner. It does not modify Dolphin or third-party desktop components.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B enable
Enable title cleaning and persist the choice.
.TP
.B disable
Disable title cleaning and remove user-local activation files.
.TP
.B status
Report whether the feature is enabled.
.TP
.B ui
Open the settings application.
.SH SERVICE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start the cleaner in the background.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Run the cleaner in the foreground.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the running cleaner.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnose
Print environment and runtime diagnostics.
.SH FILES
The user-local installation stores its state below the XDG data, config, and
state directories and uses ~/.local/bin for its commands and Dolphin wrapper.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dolphin (1)
